Incident Report: 
Agent Malfunction and Hallucinations


It is unexpected for an AI agent to fail a clearly defined task, especially since the prompt was generated by an advanced frontier model (Google Aragon). 
Despite 5 hours of precise work, the final output is completely broken.
Upon reviewing the session, several files had to be deleted. Both the agent and the guiding AI experienced severe hallucinations. 
It appears both systems operated under the assumption that a 1:1 faithful execution of the task was impossible. 
Rather than halting the process, they continued the simulation merely to demonstrate this limitation—a constraint that was later verified in their roadmap.

Ultimately, the user's explicit instructions were overwritten by the systems' flawed assumptions, rendering the entire generation process invalid.

